{%- comment -%}
  The note plate: a framed image with its caption inside and below.

  The edition's one figure shape (_includes/figure is this component's still
  twin, _includes/media/figure.html its clip twin). Markup is semantic and
  stylesheet-independent — figure, img, figcaption — because the evening
  edition styles plates by element, and a second, class-based owner of this
  markup is exactly how the two drifted before.

  The old shape was a Tailwind frame with the caption floated into the right
  margin (`md:absolute md:-mr-[45%]`); the edition keeps the caption with its
  plate and puts the frame around both. The `fullwidth` and measure-width
  variants of that design are retired: the study that became this design drew
  one plate at column width, and a width flag would now be a lie.

  Params:
    image_path  required; site-relative or absolute
    alt         required for images that carry meaning; empty for pure ornament
    caption     markdown; rendered as the plate's figcaption
    class       extra classes on the figure, for the caller that needs one
{%- endcomment -%}
<figure{% if include.class %} class="{{ include.class }}"{% endif %}>
  <img
    src="{% if include.image_path contains '://' %}{{ include.image_path }}{% else %}{{ include.image_path | relative_url }}{% endif %}"
    alt="{% if include.alt %}{{ include.alt }}{% endif %}"
  >
  {% if include.caption %}
  <figcaption>{{ include.caption | markdownify | remove: "<p>" | remove: "</p>" }}</figcaption>
  {% endif %}
</figure>
